NAME
       ping - send ICMP ECHO_REQUEST to network hosts

SYNOPSIS
       ping [-q] [-c COUNT] [-i INTERVAL] [-W TIMEOUT] HOST

DESCRIPTION
       Send ICMP echo requests to HOST (IP address, host name or URL) and print
       the round trip times, then a summary with packet loss and min/avg/max
       time. Ctrl+C stops early and still prints the summary.

OPTIONS
       -c COUNT
           stop after COUNT requests (default 4, 0 = until interrupted)

       -t
           ping until interrupted

       -i SECONDS
           wait between requests (default 1, minimum 0.2)

       -W SECONDS
           time to wait for each reply (default 2)

       -q
           print only the summary

EXAMPLES
       ping 8.8.8.8
       ping -c 10 google.com
       ping -t 1.1.1.1

SEE ALSO
       curl(1)
